abstract: >-
  An engine for building and manipulating supply-use and input-output systems:
  loading published tables from statistical offices, disaggregating sectors
  against proxy data, balancing with RAS and GRAS, transforming supply-use
  pairs into symmetric tables, projecting to a later year, and regionalising a
  national table with the location quotient family. Every method is implemented
  against the paragraph and page of the manual that specifies it, every cell
  carries whether it was observed, estimated or adjusted, and every result is
  printed together with the measured cost of the assumptions that produced it.
keywords:
  - input-output analysis
  - supply-use tables
  - regionalisation
  - location quotient
  - sector disaggregation
  - reproducible research
